---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Wanderburg Bosses Guide — Four Bosses per Land, Unlock Chain (0.9.14 EA)';
const description =
  'Wanderburg bosses: how the four-boss-per-land chain works (Green Plains → Golden Dunes), what bosses unlock, when to fight vs cash out, and the lifetime boss achievements. No invented boss names.';

const ogImage = 'https://wanderburgguide.site/images/modules/still-battle-b.jpg';
const heroSrc = '/images/modules/still-battle-b.jpg';

const lands = [
  {
    land: 'Green Plains',
    bosses: '4 bosses',
    verified: 'Verified on EN tapes',
    unlocks: 'Clears the map → next land (Golden Dunes)',
  },
  {
    land: 'Golden Dunes (the “Desert Biome” on Steam achievements)',
    bosses: '4 bosses',
    verified: 'Verified on EN tapes',
    unlocks: 'All four down → Spiderberg unlock toast (then buy)',
  },
  {
    land: 'Dusky Pines',
    bosses: 'Boss count not verified',
    verified: 'Spoken as difficulty 3, tagged 1.3× silver',
    unlocks: 'That silver tag only pays if you reach Overtime',
  },
  {
    land: 'Wasteland',
    bosses: 'Boss count not verified',
    verified: 'Called the hardest land by creators',
    unlocks: 'Skip until your kit survives a full clear',
  },
];

const bossLadder = [
  { tier: '10 bosses destroyed', rate: '50.8% of players', note: 'About two-and-a-half full Green Plains + Golden Dunes loops' },
  { tier: '25 bosses destroyed', rate: '18.9%', note: 'Regular land-cycling — Overtime runs still count the bosses you kill' },
  { tier: '50 bosses destroyed', rate: '3.7%', note: 'Grind territory' },
  { tier: '75 bosses destroyed', rate: '0.8%', note: 'Grind territory' },
  { tier: '100 bosses destroyed', rate: '0.2%', note: 'Rarest combat achievement tier' },
];

const toc = [
  { href: '#key-takeaways', label: 'Key Takeaways' },
  { href: '#boss-chain', label: 'How bosses gate the run' },
  { href: '#lands', label: 'Lands & unlock chain' },
  { href: '#fight-vs-cashout', label: 'Fight or cash out' },
  { href: '#survival', label: 'Staying alive at a boss' },
  { href: '#boss-achievements', label: 'Boss achievements' },
  { href: '#faq', label: 'FAQ' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} ogImage={ogImage} canonicalPath="/bosses/">
  <div class="editorial-hero">
    <img
      src={heroSrc}
      alt="Wanderburg battle — a boss fight at the edge of Overtime"
      width="1920"
      height="1080"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
  </div>

  <div class="editorial-layout">
    <article class="editorial-main">
      <h1>Wanderburg Bosses</h1>
      <p class="page-meta">Last Updated · Sep 13, 2026 · Early Access</p>
      <p class="editorial-intro">
        Every land ends the same way: four bosses, then the Overtime decision. Here is the verified chain — and what we
        still cannot confirm (like boss names).
      </p>

      <section class="takeaways" id="key-takeaways" aria-labelledby="takeaways-heading">
        <h2 id="takeaways-heading">Key Takeaways</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Four bosses per land</strong> — the verified loop on Green Plains and Golden Dunes.</li>
          <li>Bosses gate progression: <strong>Golden Dunes’ four bosses unlock Spiderberg</strong> (then buy with silver).</li>
          <li>Leftover boss on the field? <strong>Cash out</strong> — grinding OT next to a boss is the classic run-ender.</li>
          <li>No official boss names exist on EN tapes yet — we won’t invent them.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section" id="boss-chain">
        <h2>How do bosses gate a Wanderburg run?</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> Each land is a loop of <strong>four boss fights</strong>. Clear them and the land is
          done — the game offers the end screen <strong>or</strong> Overtime, and your next land unlocks.
        </p>
        <p>
          “You won!” — the achievement 79% of players already have — is exactly that moment: finishing a land. The
          lifetime boss ladder (10 → 25 → 50 → 75 → 100 bosses destroyed) counts across every run, Overtime included.
        </p>
        <p>
          One Chinese-language starter guide adds that beating stage bosses upgrades the castle body itself — plausible,
          but we haven’t read it on EN tape yet, so treat it as <em>to be confirmed</em>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="rankings-section" id="lands" aria-labelledby="lands-heading">
        <h2 id="lands-heading">Lands and what their bosses unlock</h2>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Land</th>
                <th>Bosses</th>
                <th>Evidence</th>
                <th>Clearing it unlocks</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {lands.map((l) => (
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>{l.land}</strong></td>
                  <td>{l.bosses}</td>
                  <td>{l.verified}</td>
                  <td>{l.unlocks}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="meta-note">
          Steam’s achievement text names the <strong>Desert Biome</strong> (68.5% unlock) and a
          <strong>Dark Forest Biome</strong> (55.8%). Creators say Dusky Pines and Wasteland — we can’t yet map those
          names onto the achievement biomes with confidence, so both are listed. See
          <a href="/achievements/">Achievements</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section" id="fight-vs-cashout">
        <h2>Four bosses down — fight on or cash out?</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> After the fourth boss, with HP intact and a clear field, <strong>Overtime pays
          better than anything else</strong> — that’s the core silver loop (<a href="/silver-farming/">Silver
          farming</a>). With a boss still alive on the field, cash out: grind tapes call that state “not great”, and the
          enemy speed-up turns a leftover boss into a run-ender.
        </p>
        <div class="decision-tree">
          <h3>Quick call</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Field clear + HP fine</strong> → enter Overtime, kite, bank silver.</li>
            <li><strong>Boss still walking</strong> → cash out. Re-fight him next run with a fuller kit.</li>
            <li><strong>Mid-fight brick (no mobility, low HP)</strong> → cash out, spend the toast, come back stronger.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section" id="survival">
        <h2>Staying alive at a boss — what’s verified</h2>
        <p>
          Bosses punish a stationary castle. The moves that consistently survive on tape are all mobility-first:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Kite, don’t facetank.</strong> Overtime-grade kits (mines while driving, ram shoves, boost) exist
            precisely because standing still loses the run.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Feed one family before the boss window.</strong> Side cannons to level 10 → Front Cannon toast is the
            standard power spike between bosses (<a href="/best-modules/">Best modules</a>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Bring mobility even on Empress.</strong> Her half-speed tax is most expensive exactly when a boss is
            chasing you — pair with ram / booster / nitro (<a href="/captains/">Captains</a>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>First-boss window is the hard part.</strong> Chinese-language guides agree the stretch before the
            first boss falls is when runs die — your kit is thinnest there. Spend early gold on the damage engine, not
            spread picks.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Two Hotfix 0.9.14 (23 Sep) changes matter at a boss: the camera <strong>zooms out slightly during boss fights</strong>,
          so a sudden change in apparent distance is the game showing you the whole arena rather than a spawn bug, and
          <strong>allied units are now immune to fire, stun and knockback</strong> — consistency, not a new power level. Larger
          enemies no longer take percentage-based damage from <strong>boss explosion damage</strong>, and stun resistances for
          Overtime enemies were adjusted, so any stun-lock plan written before 23 Sep needs re-testing in the current build.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="rankings-section" id="boss-achievements" aria-labelledby="bossach-heading">
        <h2 id="bossach-heading">Boss achievements (lifetime ladder)</h2>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Achievement</th>
                <th>Global unlock rate</th>
                <th>Note</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {bossLadder.map((b) => (
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>{b.tier}</strong></td>
                  <td>{b.rate}</td>
                  <td>{b.note}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="meta-note">
          Rates from the public Steam achievements page, Sep 2026 — they move as more players finish the tutorial
          window. Full list: <a href="/achievements/">Achievements</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section" id="faq">
        <h2>FAQ</h2>
        <h3>How many bosses are in Wanderburg?</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> Four per land. Green Plains and Golden Dunes both show the four-boss loop on tape;
          the deeper lands’ exact counts aren’t verified yet.
        </p>
        <h3>What are the boss names?</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> Not published on EN tapes or official copy we can read — so we don’t print any. Sites
          listing boss names right now are inventing them. When names appear on tape, they land here first.
        </p>
        <h3>Do bosses respawn / can I refarm them?</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> Bosses reappear every run of the same land — that’s what makes the lifetime ladder
          (10/25/50/75/100) reachable, and why Overtime kills still count. Exact respawn scheduling per land: not
          verified.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="crosslinks">
        <strong>Next:</strong>
        <a href="/silver-farming/">Silver farming</a> ·
        <a href="/unlocks/">Unlock conditions</a> ·
        <a href="/best-modules/">Best modules</a> ·
        <a href="/">Home</a>
      </div>

      <details class="still-checking">
        <summary>Still checking</summary>
        <ul>
          <li>Boss names and attack patterns — nothing readable on EN tapes yet.</li>
          <li>Boss counts for Dusky Pines / Wasteland.</li>
          <li>“Castle body upgrades on stage bosses” — CN-guide claim, needs EN tape.</li>
          <li>Achievement-name ↔ land-name mapping (Desert / Dark Forest vs Golden Dunes / Dusky Pines).</li>
        </ul>
      </details>
    </article>

    <aside class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="toc-label">On this page</p>
      <nav>
        {toc.map((item, i) => (
          <a href={item.href} class={i === 0 ? 'is-active' : undefined}>{item.label}</a>
        ))}
      </nav>
    </aside>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
